-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/SCSH> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "[Duplicate: use STK] \r\n\r\nIncludes Skelgill and Browgill Formations as separately defined: dominantly mudstone."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/SCSH> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLowerBoundaryDefinition> "Unconformably overlies the Red Gill Formation of the Dent Group."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/STK> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLowerBoundaryDefinition> "The lower boundary of the group coincides with the base of the Skelgill Mudstone Formation."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/SCSH> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasOldestAge> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/SL> .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/SCSH> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasOldestAgeValue> "443.1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/SCSH> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasPredominantAge> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/SL> .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/SCSH> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasThicknessDescription> "About 50 metres."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/SCSH> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasUpperBoundaryDefinition> "Conformably overlain by the Brathay Formation."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/SCSH> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasYoungestAge> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/SL> .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/SCSH> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasYoungestAgeValue> "432.9"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/SCSH> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Mudstone. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Llandovery Epoch (Silurian Period) (443.1-432.9 Ma BP)."@en .
